# Vertical telescope, scintillators only (mode 0), EcoMug 0.1-1000 GeV/c,
# with or without the concrete floors of the high-rise building.
#
# Used by overburden_scan.sh, which replaces the placeholders:
#   ROOF      true / false   (false = vacuum reference)
#   NSLABS    number of floors above the room
#   THICK     thickness of one floor slab in cm (G4_CONCRETE, 2.3 g/cm3)
#   NEVENTS   number of generated muons
#
# The vacuum run and the concrete runs use the SAME generation plane and the
# SAME seed (-r), so EcoMug generates the same muons in all of them and the
# rate ratio can be taken event by event.
#
# Geometry of the slabs: stacked without gaps directly above the frame
# (lower surface 1.30 m, the telescope world ends at 1.27 m). For wide
# horizontal slabs and a uniform flux on the plane, the height of the slabs
# and the gaps between the floors do not change the rate (see the comment in
# DetectorConstruction.cc), but they would make the plane much larger.
#
# Generation plane: z = 2.81 m, 1 mm above the top of 5 x 30 cm, so one
# plane serves every thickness up to 5 x 30 cm. Straight lines through both
# outer panels start within |x|,|y| < 0.69 m of the axis at this height; the
# half size of 1.2 m leaves 0.5 m for multiple scattering in the concrete.
# Check with the x0, y0 of the four-fold muons that the distribution ends
# well inside +-1.2 m.

/run/initialize

/detector/zenith  0 deg
/detector/azimuth 0 deg
/detector/geometryMode 0

/detector/roof          ROOF
/detector/roofSlabs     NSLABS
/detector/roofThickness THICK cm
/detector/roofSlabGap   0 m
/detector/roofHeight    1.30 m
/detector/roofHalfSize  2.0 m

/detector/rebuild

/muonSource/ecomug/surface     sky
/muonSource/ecomug/skySizeX    2.4 m
/muonSource/ecomug/skySizeY    2.4 m
/muonSource/ecomug/skyCenter   0 0 2.81 m
/muonSource/ecomug/minMomentum 0.1 GeV
/muonSource/ecomug/maxMomentum 1000 GeV

/run/beamOn NEVENTS
